This patch accomplishes the following:

- If you polymorph into a silver hating creature, you will receive burns
  of 1hp for every silver item that you are wearing or wielding, and you
  will lose rnd(12) hp for every item that is cursed or cannot be  
removed (cursed gloves and whatnot.)
- If you continue wearing these things, every turn will result in rnd(6)
  * # of silver items damage.
- You will not be able to wield, pick up, or wear silver things for the
  duration of your polymorph, and you will receive a small burn for     
trying each of these things.

It made sense to me -- for kicks, I had a Wizard mode character
polymorph into a balrog, and he was wielding two silver sabers, and
wearing two silver rings and he was whacking away at everyone :)

Sample output:

You turn into a balrog!
You feel a searing sting in your right foreclaw!
But you can't drop the silver silver saber in it!
The skin on your foreclaw burns away!  Your left foreclaw is on fire!
But the silver ring on your foreclaw won't come off!
The skin on your foreclaw burns away!  Your right foreclaw burns!
But the silver ring on your foreclaw won't come off!
The skin on your foreclaw burns away!
Your silver shield burns your foreclaw!
You can't drop it! The skin on your foreclaw burns away.

also, while wearing cursed silver items as a silver-fearing monster:

Your body is scorched by the silver you are wearing!

BTW, the patch also accounts for un-polymorphing in the middle of the
silver burn process. What do you guys think?

--
Joshua Kwan

